      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-244592",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/85/851d6135ff3984bccf536927316b6b12beb9ec73ba377119c94ae0ebc15745c3.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, we have\n$\\frac{EG}{AC} = \\frac{3}{2}$.\n\nProve that $\u2220A\u2245\u2220E$.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $\\frac{EG}{AC} = \\frac{3}{2}$ | Given |\n| 2 | $\\frac{EF}{AB} = \\frac{FG}{BC} = \\frac{3}{2}$ | Substitution |\n| 3 | $\\frac{EF}{AB} = \\frac{FG}{BC} = \\frac{EG}{AC}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| 4 | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |\n| 5 | $\u2220A\u2245\u2220E$ | {{field-4}} |"
